      Title: Chocolate Chip Cookies
 Categories: Cookies, Desserts
      Yield: 36 servings

      1 c  Butter, softened                    1 ts Vanilla extract
    3/4 c  Granulated sugar                2 1/4 c  All-purpose flour
    3/4 c  Brown sugar, packed                 1 ts Baking soda
      2    Eggs                                1 ts Salt
      2 c  Semisweet chocolate chips
      1 c  Chopped walnuts
           -optional

  Preheat oven to 375 F. Cream butter, granulated sugar and brown sugar
  until fluffy. Beat in eggs and vanilla.

  Combine flour, baking soda and salt; gradually add to the butter mixture.
  Stir in chocolate chips and nuts. Drop by rounded tablespoons onto
  ungreased baking sheets, about 2 inches apart.

  Bake 9 to 11 minutes or until golden brown. Cool on wire racks.

MMMMM

MMMMM----- Recipe via Meal-Master (tm) v8.05

      Title: Chicken Vegetable Soup
 Categories: Soups, Poultry, Main dish
      Yield: 6 servings

      1 lb Boneless skinless chicken breasts
      2 T  Olive oil
      1 lg Onion, chopped
      2    Carrots, sliced
      2    Celery ribs, sliced
      2    Garlic cloves, minced
      6 c  Chicken broth
      1 cn Diced tomatoes (14 oz)
      2    Potatoes, peeled and cubed
      1 ts Dried thyme
      1    Bay leaf
    1/2 c  Frozen peas
           Salt and pepper to taste

MMMMM-------------------------TOPPING-----------------------------
      2 T  Fresh parsley, chopped
    1/4 c  Parmesan cheese, grated

  Cut chicken into 1-inch pieces. Heat oil in a large pot and brown the
  chicken; remove and set aside.

  Saute onion, carrots and celery in the same pot for 5 minutes. Add
  garlic, broth, tomatoes, potatoes, thyme and bay leaf. Bring to a boil,
  reduce heat and simmer 20 minutes.

  Return chicken to the pot, add peas and simmer 10 minutes longer. Season
  with salt and pepper. Remove bay leaf and serve sprinkled with parsley
  and Parmesan.

MMMMM

MMMMM----- Recipe via Meal-Master (tm) v8.05

      Title: Quarkauflauf mit Kirschen
 Categories: Dessert, Auflauf, Vegetarisch
      Yield: 4 Portionen

    500 g  Magerquark
      3    Eier
     80 g  Zucker
      1 pk Vanillezucker
     50 g  Grieß
      1    Zitrone, Schale davon
    350 g  Sauerkirschen (Glas), abgetropft
     20 g  Butter

  Den Backofen auf 180 Grad vorheizen. Eine Auflaufform mit Butter
  ausfetten.

  Quark, Eier, Zucker, Vanillezucker, Grieß und Zitronenschale glatt
  rühren. Die Kirschen unterheben und die Masse in die Form füllen.

  Etwa 40 Minuten goldbraun backen. Warm oder kalt servieren.

MMMMM
